IMPORT prelude

-- Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 (Singapore) -- which exemption clauses the Act strikes down, which survive only if reasonable,
-- and which it leaves alone: ss 1(3), 2, 3, 4, 6, 7(3A), 11(5), 12, 26, 27 and First Schedule paragraphs 1 and 4.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/UCTA1977.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and is dated 31.12.2021; the latest amendment
-- annotated in the body is [44/96] (s 7(3A), (4)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the core controls on contract
-- terms, the meaning of "deals as consumer", and the two cross-border escapes (international supply contracts, choice of law).
-- Not encoded: notices that are not contract terms (s 2 covers them but the module models contract terms only), guarantees of
-- consumer goods (s 5), s 7 beyond the title rule in subsection (3A), effect of breach (s 9), secondary contracts (s 10), the
-- content of the reasonableness test (s 11(1)-(4), Second Schedule) -- reasonableness is taken as a finding --, varieties of
-- exemption clause (s 13), sea carriage of passengers (s 28), the statutory saving (s 29), the transitional date (s 30(2)), and
-- First Schedule paragraphs 2 and 3 (shipping).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977 -- exemption clauses`

-- The liability a contract term tries to exclude or restrict.
DECLARE Liability IS ONE OF
    `death or personal injury from negligence`
    `other loss from negligence`
    `breach of contract`
    `an indemnity given by the other party`
    `title to goods sold`
    `description, quality or fitness of goods sold`

-- What the Act does to the term.
DECLARE Control IS ONE OF
    `cannot be excluded`
    `excludable only so far as reasonable`
    `not controlled by the Act`

-- s 11(5): "It is for those claiming that a contract term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness to show that
-- it does." The field `shown reasonable by the party relying on it` is therefore FALSE unless that party has proved it.
DECLARE `Exemption clause` HAS
    `liability excluded` IS A Liability
    `liability arises in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party deals as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `on the excluding party's written standard terms` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an insurance, land, IP, company or securities contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in a contract of employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other party is the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an international supply contract` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Singapore law governs only by choice of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
    `shown reasonable by the party relying on it` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `12 -- dealing as consumer`

-- s 12(1): a party "deals as consumer" if (a) "he neither makes the contract in the course of a business nor holds himself out
-- as doing so"; (b) "the other party does make the contract in the course of a business"; and (c) for sale of goods,
-- hire-purchase or s 7 contracts, the goods "are of a type ordinarily supplied for private use or consumption".
-- s 12(2): "on a sale by auction or by competitive tender the buyer is not in any circumstances to be regarded as dealing as
-- consumer". s 12(3): it is for those claiming that a party does not deal as consumer to show that he does not (not modelled
-- beyond this note).
GIVEN `acts in the course of a business or holds himself out as doing so` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `counterparty acts in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `goods pass under the contract` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `goods ordinarily supplied for private use` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `buyer at auction or competitive tender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `deals as consumer` IF
        (NOT `acts in the course of a business or holds himself out as doing so`)
    AND `counterparty acts in the course of a business`
    AND ((NOT `goods pass under the contract`) OR `goods ordinarily supplied for private use`)
    AND (NOT `buyer at auction or competitive tender`)

§§ `26 -- international supply contracts`

-- s 26(1): the limits "do not apply to liability arising under such a contract as is described in subsection (3)"; (2) not
-- subject to reasonableness under s 3 or 4. (3) (a) a sale of goods or a contract under which possession or ownership of goods
-- passes, and (b) "made by parties whose places of business (or, if they have none, habitual residences) are in the territories
-- of different States". (4) only if (a) the goods are in carriage, or will be carried, between States; (b) offer and acceptance
-- were done in different States; or (c) delivery is to a State other than where those acts were done.
GIVEN `a contract under which goods pass` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `parties based in different States` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `goods carried from one State to another` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `offer and acceptance in different States` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `delivery to another State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an international supply contract` IF
        `a contract under which goods pass`
    AND `parties based in different States`
    AND (   `goods carried from one State to another`
         OR `offer and acceptance in different States`
         OR `delivery to another State`)

§§ `27 -- choice of law`

-- s 27(1): where Singapore law is the proper law "only by choice of the parties", ss 2 to 7 do not operate (modelled in the
-- Exemption clause record). s 27(2): the Act has effect "notwithstanding any contract term which applies or purports to apply
-- the law of some country outside Singapore" where (a) the term was imposed "wholly or mainly for the purpose of enabling the
-- party imposing it to evade the operation of this Act"; or (b) one party dealt as consumer, "was then habitually resident in
-- Singapore, and the essential steps necessary for the making of the contract were taken there".
GIVEN `foreign law imposed mainly to evade the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a party dealt as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `that party habitually resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `essential steps taken in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies despite a foreign choice of law` IF
       `foreign law imposed mainly to evade the Act`
    OR (    `a party dealt as consumer`
        AND `that party habitually resident in Singapore`
        AND `essential steps taken in Singapore`)

§§ `1(3), 2, 3, 4 and First Schedule -- reach of the negligence and contract controls`

-- s 1(3): ss 2 to 7 apply (except as s 6(4) says) "only to business liability". First Schedule para 1: "Sections 2 to 4 do not
-- extend to" (a) insurance; (b) interests in land; (c) intellectual property; (d) formation, dissolution or constitution of a
-- company; (e) securities.
GIVEN `the clause` IS AN `Exemption clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 2 to 4 reach the clause` IF
        `the clause`'s `liability arises in the course of a business`
    AND (NOT `the clause`'s `in an insurance, land, IP, company or securities contract`)

-- First Schedule para 4: "Subsections (1) and (2) of section 2 do not extend to a contract of employment, except in favour of
-- the employee."
GIVEN `the clause` IS AN `Exemption clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 2 reaches the clause` IF
        `sections 2 to 4 reach the clause` `the clause`
    AND (   (NOT `the clause`'s `in a contract of employment`)
         OR `the clause`'s `the other party is the employee`)

-- s 3(1): applies "where one of them deals as consumer or on the other's written standard terms of business".
GIVEN `the clause` IS AN `Exemption clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 3 reaches the clause` IF
        `sections 2 to 4 reach the clause` `the clause`
    AND (   `the clause`'s `the other party deals as consumer`
         OR `the clause`'s `on the excluding party's written standard terms`)

-- s 4(1): "A person dealing as consumer cannot by reference to any contract term be made to indemnify another person ...
-- except in so far as the contract term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness."
GIVEN `the clause` IS AN `Exemption clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4 reaches the clause` IF
        `sections 2 to 4 reach the clause` `the clause`
    AND `the clause`'s `the other party deals as consumer`

§§ `2, 3, 4, 6, 26(1), 27(1) -- what the Act does to the clause`

-- s 2(1): no exclusion of liability "for death or personal injury resulting from negligence". s 2(2): other loss or damage only
-- "in so far as the term or notice satisfies the requirement of reasonableness". s 3(2): breach of contract, reasonableness.
-- s 4(1): consumer indemnity, reasonableness.
-- s 6(1): liability under s 12 of the Sale of Goods Act 1979 (title) "cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any
-- contract term". s 6(2): as against a consumer, ss 13-15 (description, quality, fitness) cannot be excluded; s 6(3): otherwise
-- only so far as reasonable. s 6(4): s 6 liabilities "are not only the business liabilities defined by section 1(3), but include
-- those arising under any contract of sale of goods". The First Schedule para 1 exceptions reach ss 2 to 4 (and 7), not s 6.
-- s 26(1) and s 27(1) take the clause outside the Act altogether.
GIVEN `the clause` IS AN `Exemption clause`
GIVETH A Control
DECIDE `the Act's control over the clause` IS
    IF     `the clause`'s `in an international supply contract`
        OR `the clause`'s `Singapore law governs only by choice of the parties`
    THEN `not controlled by the Act`
    ELSE `the control by liability` `the clause`

GIVEN `the clause` IS AN `Exemption clause`
GIVETH A Control
DECIDE `the control by liability` IS
    CONSIDER `the clause`'s `liability excluded`
    WHEN `death or personal injury from negligence` THEN
        `control if reached` (`section 2 reaches the clause` `the clause`) `cannot be excluded`
    WHEN `other loss from negligence` THEN
        `control if reached` (`section 2 reaches the clause` `the clause`) `excludable only so far as reasonable`
    WHEN `breach of contract` THEN
        `control if reached` (`section 3 reaches the clause` `the clause`) `excludable only so far as reasonable`
    WHEN `an indemnity given by the other party` THEN
        `control if reached` (`section 4 reaches the clause` `the clause`) `excludable only so far as reasonable`
    WHEN `title to goods sold` THEN `cannot be excluded`
    WHEN `description, quality or fitness of goods sold` THEN
        `consumer or not` (`the clause`'s `the other party deals as consumer`)

GIVEN `reached` IS A BOOLEAN, `the control` IS A Control
GIVETH A Control
DECIDE `control if reached` IS
    IF `reached` THEN `the control` ELSE `not controlled by the Act`

GIVEN `against a consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Control
DECIDE `consumer or not` IS
    IF `against a consumer` THEN `cannot be excluded` ELSE `excludable only so far as reasonable`

-- Whether the clause can be relied on against the other party: a void exclusion never; a reasonableness-controlled one only if
-- the party relying on it has shown it reasonable (s 11(5)); an uncontrolled one always (as far as this Act goes).
GIVEN `the clause` IS AN `Exemption clause`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the clause can be relied on` IF
    CONSIDER `the Act's control over the clause` `the clause`
    WHEN `cannot be excluded` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `excludable only so far as reasonable` THEN `the clause`'s `shown reasonable by the party relying on it`
    WHEN `not controlled by the Act` THEN TRUE

§§ `7(3A) -- title in other contracts under which goods pass`

-- s 7(3A): "Liability for breach of the obligations arising under section 2 of the Supply of Goods Act 1982 (implied terms about
-- title, etc. ...) cannot be excluded or restricted by reference to any such term." s 7(4): otherwise title and quiet possession
-- only so far as reasonable "in a case to which subsection (3A) does not apply". This helper assumes s 7 is otherwise engaged:
-- business liability (s 1(3)), no First Schedule exception, no s 26 or s 27(1) escape.
GIVEN `the Supply of Goods Act 1982 s 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Control
DECIDE `control over a title exclusion in a supply contract` IS
    IF `the Supply of Goods Act 1982 s 2 applies` THEN `cannot be excluded` ELSE `excludable only so far as reasonable`
